# Tethering train gate (target/a52sxq/patches/tethering_trains, see k4-tethering-gate). On an update boot this file's
# action runs after the evidence capture in a52sxq_mainline.rc (same trigger, that file sorts first) and before
# netbpfload.rc's load-bpf-programs action starts the loader. Blocking, ~0.2 s, update boots only.
on load-bpf-programs && property:apexd.packages.updated=true
    exec u:r:k4apexdm:s0 root root -- /system/bin/sh /system/bin/k4-tethering-gate

# A gap was found: take the stock revert path instead of the crash loop. init may set sys.init.* itself; apexd
# (ApexdLifecycle::WaitForBootStatus) polls sys.init.updatable_crashing every 10 s while a staged session is active,
# logs "Native process 'netd' is crashing. Attempting a revert", reverts the session and reboots.
on property:sys.k4.tethering_gap=*
    setprop sys.init.updatable_crashing_process_name netd
    setprop sys.init.updatable_crashing 1
